WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.323 --> 00:00:02.906
(serene music)

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.247
- It was always I can't, you
shouldn't, don't do this.

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:12.423
You know, it's impossible.

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:17.331
It's too challenging, it's too difficult.

00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:21.146
They're saying that I can't
before I even attempt to try.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:23.306
That's not the way to live.

00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:25.806
(engine revs)

00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:28.532
- I was up doing a wheelie on the freeway.

00:00:28.532 --> 00:00:31.541
I went to try to get away
from the police officer.

00:00:31.541 --> 00:00:35.094
Car merged into my lane and
I hit the center divider.

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:36.843
This decision to do that actually

00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:40.093
cost me the ability to ever walk again.

00:00:43.221 --> 00:00:45.441
When I got out of the
hospital after my injury

00:00:45.441 --> 00:00:47.740
I realized everybody
that was in a wheelchair

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.769
was either wearing these
elastic waistband pants

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:53.496
or getting by wearing sweatpants and,

00:00:53.496 --> 00:00:57.496
that's when I realized
hey, these guys need help.

00:01:00.194 --> 00:01:02.351
We're in our Los Angeles,
California factory,

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:06.689
where we manufacture and
make my Ability Jeans.

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:08.013
Normal jeans don't fit us.

00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:11.399
We can't access back pockets
and buttons and rivets

00:01:11.399 --> 00:01:13.839
can cause pressure source
for people in wheelchairs.

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.515
So we don't have no rear pockets,

00:01:15.515 --> 00:01:17.765
smooth surface in the back.

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:21.357
We take all things in
consideration, you know.

00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:22.924
The durability of 'em.

00:01:22.924 --> 00:01:27.150
Our belt loop being stronger
so when you pull your pants up

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.205
by the belt loop they don't break.

00:01:29.205 --> 00:01:31.337
But in a way that they don't stand out.

00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:35.504
They look as great as any
other jeans on the market.

00:01:36.984 --> 00:01:40.077
They told me I would never walk again.

00:01:40.077 --> 00:01:43.266
I was like, “Well, I will be able
to ride motorcycles, right?”

00:01:43.266 --> 00:01:45.987
They said my life doing that was over.

00:01:45.987 --> 00:01:48.709
And that was the reason
why I said it wasn't

00:01:48.709 --> 00:01:50.842
and I'm gonna build something that I am

00:01:50.842 --> 00:01:53.259
and gonna be able to ride again.

00:01:55.355 --> 00:01:57.503
You ride for that freedom, you know?

00:01:57.503 --> 00:01:59.684
I look at the road, I
look at what's around me.

00:01:59.684 --> 00:02:02.136
I feel the throttle and I ride.

00:02:02.136 --> 00:02:05.167
I don't look over and say,
“Oh, there's my wheelchair.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.512
I gotta get back to that when I'm, no.

00:02:07.512 --> 00:02:09.844
For the moment I'm
riding and it's freedom.

00:02:09.844 --> 00:02:13.594
There ain't nothing that
can compare to that.

